# Validation case 3: Structural stall
#
# The Spec standard configuration has 4 ALU reservation stations.
# Six ADDs simultaneously issue into the pool, and a single-entry
# instruction queue (configured by the test, not the trace) keeps
# the front-end from outpacing the issue stage. The first four
# ADDs fill the RS slots; the remaining two must wait until a slot
# frees through dispatch. That wait is the structural stall the
# StructuralStalls statistic counts.
#
# Program:
#   R0 = R0 + R1
#   R1 = R0 + R0
#   R2 = R0 + R0
#   R3 = R0 + R0
#   R4 = R0 + R0
#   R5 = R0 + R0
#
# Expected final state (numerically uninteresting; what matters
# is that all six retired and StructuralStalls > 0):
#   R0 = R1 = R2 = R3 = R4 = R5
ADD R0, R0, R1
ADD R1, R0, R0
ADD R2, R0, R0
ADD R3, R0, R0
ADD R4, R0, R0
ADD R5, R0, R0
i
